    {
        "record_type": "comment",
        "text": "Darz, this is a thoughtful and ambitious approach to the constitutional coordination of institutional knowledge!\n \nYour distinction between research, evidence, engineering, evaluation, governance and stewardship raises an important question about how knowledge becomes consequential within institutions!\n \nOne area I find particularly worth examining is the relationship between knowledge correction and institutional decision-making:\n \nWhen evidence, assumptions or conclusions are legitimately challenged or corrected, how can we establish that those corrections reach the governing decision, influence it where justified and remain effective before the opportunity for meaningful intervention is lost?\n \nPreserving knowledge and its provenance is essential. Demonstrating that justified correction can influence consequential decisions is a further evidentiary question!\n \nI look forward to seeing how CKCA develops through its documentary review.\n \nThank you for contributing to this important discussion Darz!🌹🤝",
        "author": "Evelyne-Claudia Y.",
        "date": "2026-11-19T11:23:09.791Z",
        "engagement": {
            "likes": 0,
            "comments": 0,
            "shares": 0,
            "reactions": []
        },
